<gpx version="1.1" creator="Flores Race Planner (pipeline/export_gpx.py)" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1 http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1/gpx.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <name>S02 Wae Rebo and the south coast of Manggarai</name>
    <desc>Section 02 of the Flores Race traverse: The flagship cultural checkpoint, on foot with the bike. 164.7 km, +4151 m / -4447 m, starts at km 102 of the course.</desc>
    <link href="https://github.com/technicaloutdoor/Flores-Race"><text>Flores Race Planner</text></link>
    <time>2026-09-05T06:27:57Z</time>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="-8.648640" lon="120.010760">
    <ele>345.9</ele>
    <name>Werang</name>
    <desc>km 0.0 | kind: village | resupply: basic | water: unreliable | sleep: homestay -- Capital of Sano Nggoang kecamatan: parish church (Santo Klaus), police post, camat office, schools. The practical resupply stop after the lake.</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.846000" lon="120.308000">
    <ele>59.7</ele>
    <name>Dintor</name>
    <desc>km 78.4 | kind: village | resupply: minimal | water: unreliable | sleep: none | position approximate -- South-coast village in Desa Satar Ruwuk on the Wae Nakeng-Nangalili-Borik-Dintor-Denge coastal track. Coordinates are a reasoned placement from route descriptions (no named source pin found); flagged for scouting.</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.808000" lon="120.302000">
    <ele>481.4</ele>
    <name>Denge</name>
    <desc>km 84.8 | kind: trailhead | resupply: minimal | water: unreliable | sleep: homestay | position approximate -- Last village reachable by road/motorbike before the Wae Rebo trek (about 8 km, +700 m, 2.5-3 h on foot). Coordinates placed by interpolation from route descriptions (~6 km from Dintor, ~7-9 km from Wae Rebo) and cross-ch</desc>
    <sym>Trail Head</sym>
    <type>anchor/trailhead</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.770000" lon="120.284170">
    <ele>1115.9</ele>
    <name>Wae Rebo</name>
    <desc>km 92.1 | kind: checkpoint | resupply: minimal | water: unreliable | sleep: homestay -- Cultural checkpoint; UNESCO Asia-Pacific award village. All visitors sleep and eat inside the mbaru niang under the village's own homestay system -- a race stop here means income for the community by design. Requires an </desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>anchor/checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.730920" lon="120.381590">
    <ele>464.5</ele>
    <name>Todo</name>
    <desc>km 144.9 | kind: village | resupply: minimal | water: unreliable | sleep: none -- Former seat of the Manggarai kingdom; day-trip village, no lodging found. Confirmed by five independent Overture/OSM points (church, clinic, tourism tag, school) clustered within 1.5 km.</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.811670" lon="120.420020">
    <ele>49.0</ele>
    <name>Iteng</name>
    <desc>km 164.7 | kind: village | resupply: basic | water: unreliable | sleep: none -- Capital of Satar Mese kecamatan, on the south coast (a beach point is tagged at the village itself). Has a market (pasar Iteng), a Catholic parish, a health centre and schools -- the practical resupply between Todo and R</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.625900" lon="119.997600">
    <ele>442.7</ele>
    <name>Cunca Rami waterfall</name>
    <desc>[highlight, hike-a-bike, position approximate] A ~30 m waterfall deep in the Mbeliling forest reserve, near Wae Lolos village; local sources put it around 1,200 m but the DEM at this approximate fix reads ~800 m -- location needs a field GPS fix.</desc>
    <sym>Scenic Area</sym>
    <type>poi/waterfall</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.730920" lon="120.381590">
    <ele>464.5</ele>
    <name>Todo</name>
    <desc>[anchor] Former seat of the Manggarai kingdom, with the oldest mbaru niang (conical drum house) in the regency and a genealogy said to trace Manggarai's first king; a day-trip village, not set up for overnight stays.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/traditional-village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.770000" lon="120.284170">
    <ele>1115.9</ele>
    <name>Wae Rebo</name>
    <desc>[anchor, hike-a-bike] Seven cone-shaped mbaru niang houses ringing a mountain clearing at ~1,100-1,200 m, reached only on foot; winner of the 2012 UNESCO Asia-Pacific Award for Cultural Heritage Conservation. Flores' most famous traditional village and the race's flagship cultural checkpoint.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/traditional-village</type>
  </wpt>
